{
  "bioavailability_prediction": "high",
  "confidence": "high",
  "revision_action": "keep",
  "supportive_card_ids": ["C01","C02","C05","C13","C15","C20","C21","C46","C74","C28","C29","C167","C199","C201","C210","C227","C245"],
  "contradictory_card_ids": [],
  "prediction_basis_card_ids": ["C01","C02","C05","C13","C15","C20","C21","C46","C167","C199","C201","C210","C227","C245"],
  "claims": [
    {
      "claim": "The query is ertugliflozin, whose bridged dioxabicyclo[3.2.1]octane triol core and 4-ethoxybenzyl/chlorophenyl substitution are very close to tofogliflozin; tofogliflozin has human absolute oral bioavailability of about 97.5% measured by oral 20 mg dosing with concomitant IV microdosing, far above the 20% threshold.",
      "card_ids": ["C01","C02","C05","C13","C15","C20","C21","C46","C74"]
    },
    {
      "claim": "Tofogliflozin mass-balance data show only 0.9% parent recovery in feces, indicating near-complete absorption, and animal F values of 85% in monkeys and 75% in mice support high oral bioavailability for this structural class.",
      "card_ids": ["C05","C28","C29"]
    },
    {
      "claim": "For the close analog dapagliflozin, a 50 mg oral solution in healthy subjects gave at least 75% systemic absorption within 24 h based on urinary recovery of total radioactivity, and Caco-2 data show good permeability with only weak P-gp substrate activity, consistent with high F.",
      "card_ids": ["C167","C199","C201","C210"]
    },
    {
      "claim": "L6 hepatic records do not provide affirmative low-F evidence: dapagliflozin was hardly metabolized in human hepatocytes and was the most stable in human hepatocytes among species tested, CYP oxidation is a minor route (<10%), and the ertugliflozin-family M5c glucuronide formation CLint values (34.7 µL/min/mg with BSA; 9.16 without BSA) are moderate in vitro intrinsic clearances for one glucuronidation pathway and do not quantify hepatic first-pass extraction.",
      "card_ids": ["C227","C245","C249","C270","C244","C238","C237","C269","C266"]
    },
    {
      "claim": "Records describing extensive glucuronidation for dapagliflozin are mechanistic metabolic-fate observations, not direct oral-bioavailability outcomes, and do not establish F < 20%.",
      "card_ids": ["C246","C252","C229"]
    }
  ],
  "new_evidence_assessment": [
    {
      "family": "hepatic_clearance_metabolic_stability",
      "applicability": "moderate",
      "direction": "neutral_or_unclear",
      "decision_effect": "no_change",
      "card_ids": ["C227","C229","C237","C238","C244","C245","C246","C249","C252","C266","C269","C270"]
    }
  ],
  "evidence_gaps": [
    "No direct absolute oral bioavailability measurement for ertugliflozin is present in the supplied records; the high prediction rests on the very close tofogliflozin analog and dapagliflozin absorption/permeability/metabolic-stability records.",
    "No query-specific fasted-state PK record is supplied; the fasted condition is inferred to be compatible with the high tofogliflozin F and related SGLT2 fed/fasted AUC comparability, but not directly demonstrated.",
    "L6 hepatic-clearance records are mostly for dapagliflozin, tofogliflozin, luseogliflozin, empagliflozin, DWP16001, or the ertugliflozin glucuronide (M5c), not the parent ertugliflozin; no hepatic extraction or first-pass quantification is provided.",
    "The M5c formation CLint values are for one glucuronidation pathway and lack the protein-binding and hepatic-blood-flow context needed to estimate extraction.",
    "No query-specific intestinal metabolism or efflux records are supplied; L5 records are for dapagliflozin and are mechanistic."
  ],
  "decision_summary": "Predicted high because the query is ertugliflozin, structurally very close to tofogliflozin whose human absolute oral bioavailability is ~97.5%; L4/L5/L6 add supportive absorption, permeability, and metabolic-stability context from dapagliflozin and show no affirmative low-F evidence. L6 hepatic clearance/metabolic-stability records are mechanistic, mostly for analogs or the M5c glucuronide, and do not overturn the high prediction."
}

